==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|yi|וויגריש}}, from {{der|en|ru|вы́игрыш||winnings}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-vigorish.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} A [[charge]] taken on [[bet]]s, as by a [[bookie]] or gambling establishment.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1984|title=Craps|author=John Patrick|isbn=9780930911003|page=11|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=klWntKWFWvQC&lpg=PA11|passage=The house sets vigs on any game they allow you to bet on.  It is your responsibility to play only those games where the vig is not prohibitive.  Let's take one more look at how '''vigorish''' works for the house.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Wayne L. Winston|title=Mathletics: How Gamblers, Managers, and Sports Enthusiasts Use Mathematics|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=QLI3JJ9CD5QC&pg=PA256|page=256|passage=The bookmaker's mean profit per dollar bet is called '''vigorish''' or “the vig.” In our example, 11 + 11 = $22 is bet, and the bookmaker wins $1 so the vig is 1/22 = 4.5%.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} The [[interest]] on a [[loan]] of money, especially for loans made by a [[usurer]] or [[loan shark]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976|title=The Crime Society|editors=Ianni, Francis A. J.; Reuss-Ianni, Elizabeth|chapter=The Loan-Shark Racket|page=217|passage=His clients included wealthy women who possessed jewelry of great value, a fact which did not escape the loan shark.  When it became apparent that the hairdresser could not meet his substantial '''vigorish''' payments, he was pressed into service as a "fingerman" for a burglary ring.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=Everybody Does Business|author=Harry Brooks|isbn=9781483675237|page=356|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=cVJmAwAAQBAJ&pg=PT356|passage=They lend you a thousand and call it a bone. It cost a hundred a week '''vigorish''' to borrow the bone.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|slang}} An amount owed on account of or payment of a bookie's charge or of interest.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[commission]] or similar extra charge.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|year_published=2005|title=Audrey Hepburn, An Elegant Spirit|author=w:Sean Hepburn Ferrer|isbn=9780671024796|page=216|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Xn8wjtoVspQC&pg=PT85|passage=I was asking a man who had never bent a rule in his entire life to do it once.  This wasn't Italy or France, where such miracles are possible with a little political '''vigorish'''. This was Switzerland, where nothing like this ever happens.}}

